        <h3><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-warn"/></svg> macOS will say the developer cannot be verified</h3>
        <p>Topics is signed ad-hoc rather than with a paid Apple Developer certificate, so the first launch is blocked. Since macOS Sequoia the old control-click trick no longer works: Settings is the only route, and it takes about fifteen seconds.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Open the app once and dismiss the dialog that says <b>"Apple could not verify Topics is free of malware"</b>.</li>
          <li>Go to <b>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security</b> and scroll to the bottom.</li>
          <li>Next to <b>"Topics was blocked to protect your Mac"</b>, press <b>Open Anyway</b> and confirm.</li>
